# Review is required on the paths where a merge means code execution, not
# content. A bad wiki page renders wrong and lint usually catches it; a bad
# script runs on the harness droplet with the API keys in its environment,
# and a bad workflow runs in CI with contents: write on this repo.
#
# The 3,700 content pages are deliberately NOT covered. They change hundreds
# at a time in normal enrichment batches, and requiring review on those would
# make the rule noise that gets clicked through — which is how a rule stops
# protecting the paths that actually matter.

/scripts/            @dsporcaro
/deploy/             @dsporcaro
/.github/            @dsporcaro
/mkdocs.yml          @dsporcaro
/requirements-docs.txt  @dsporcaro
/CLAUDE.md           @dsporcaro
